===Income Calculation===
Circles multiplier determines how much score you get after any circle completes a revolution.

Before prestige, your score income is determined by this formula:

 '''ⵙ/second''' = ⵙ/Revolution * [Sum of all Circles' Revolutions/second]
 '''ⵙ/Revolution''' = ([Product of all Circles' Mults] * P.Mult)^Common Exponent
Common exponent is influenced by many factors in the game so a formula wouldn't be easy to follow.

===Circle Stats===
Each circle has three critical stats:
# '''Revolution Speed''': The speed at which the circle completes its revolution.
# '''Asc. Power''': Ascension Power, which serves as a multiplier for Mult Gain on circle ascension.
# '''Mult Gain''': The amount of the corresponding color multiplier added with each lap.
To check circle stats, you need to have "show tooltip" enabled in settings then press and hold on circle.

=='''Upgrading'''==
Each circle can be upgraded using the Score earned from completing laps. Basic upgrades, referred to as Buyables, increase the circle's level and improve its speed.<br>
Each circle can be upgraded to a maximum of 100+(amount of ascensions x10) levels before needing to be ascended.  The maximum level of each buyable increases by 10 per ascension.<br>
Generally, the smaller circles are more efficient to buy than to buy a bigger circle, prioritize upgrading smaller circle that you can afford, and wait until the price difference between the bigger and smaller circles has disappeared before buying them.

====Circle Upgrade Cost====
Cost multiplier of each circle is increased by +0.1 each time it ascends. After first ascension red circle will have cost multiplier of 1.3 and 1.4 after the second ascension.<br>
Circles initial price after ascension (cost at level 0) will be the same as the cost at level 100 before ascension.<br>

So, for example, the cost of a orange circle at level 10 after one ascension can be calculated as follows:
 Orange Asc. #1 Lv10 Cost
 = 100 * (1.24 ^ 100) * (1.34 ^ 10) ⵙ
 = 100 * 2,198,712,860 * 18.66 ⵙ
 = 4,104,086,450,000 ⵙ 
 ≈ 4.1e12 ⵙ

=='''Ascension'''==
After circle is upgraded to its current level cap, it can then be ascended.

Ascending resets a circle to level 5, multiplies its Mult Gain by the Ascension Power, and raises its level cap by 10. <br>
This allows for increased Mult Gain per revolution and Lap Speed, but drastically drops lap speed due to the missing levels.
